{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1206926-how-to-weaken-a-defining-intimacy","id":1206926,"title":"How to weaken a defining Intimacy?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-14T10:04:33-07:00","id":1206926,"title":"How to weaken a defining Intimacy?","content":"Only recently got into Exalted 3rrd edition spent years avoiding it being butthurt on some of the directions things went in.<br /> <br /> cant find any charms that will really help you with weakening a defining intimacy.<br /> <br /> to help do that you need to create a new intimacy.<br /> <br /> but you caqnt do that because a defining intimacy bar's intimacys that disagree with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 04-14-2018, 01:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T10:22:38-07:00","id":1206936,"title":"","content":"To weaken a defining intimacy, you only need them to have a major intimacy that opposes it, not defining.<br /> <br /> Of course, how likely is it that they'll have a major intimacy that opposes their defining intimacy? Not likely. Though it is possible.<br /> For example, if an Immaculate Monk had a defining intimacy of &quot;All Anathema are evil&quot; and a Major Intimacy to &quot;my friend Righteous Fox&quot;, but then learns that Righteous Fox is an anathema, you could use this to weaken their belief that &quot;All Anathema are evil.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now, if they don't have any intimacies that oppose their defining intimacy at all... that's very difficult.<br /> <br /> What you'd need to do is give them a minor intimacy that opposes their defining intimacy. They'll get +4 Resolve from the Defining Intimacy, which makes it difficult, but if you've got a huge social pool it's doable. They can also spend a WP to resist getting that minor intimacy though.<br /> <br /> But if they don't, you can then increase that minor intimacy to major... if they've got another minor intimacy that supports it. So you might have to give them two! Increasing a minor intimacy to major can't be resisted with a WP, but does require stronger evidence than what gave them the minor intimacy in the first place.<br /> <br /> Once they've got a major intimacy that opposes their defining intimacy, then you can roll to weaken their defining intimacy. Though they can resist with 1 wp.<br /> <br /> So... in short, convincing Pelleps Delled that Anathema are not so evil is very, very difficult. You can't just roll dice at him.<br /> <br /> In order to weaken someone's defining beliefs that they've built their entire life on, you need to find something else they care about, which contradicts it. <br /> <br /> <br /> In terms of charms, your best bet are charms that give them minor intimacies, of which there are a small number. And of course, Fulminating Word, which means they have to spend 2wp instead of 1 to resist getting a minor intimacy or having their defining intimacy weakened.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T10:22:55-07:00","id":1206937,"title":"","content":"If you want to convince me that pretty boy are sexier than bear, you better bring your A-game at social skills instead of spending some motes expecting me to kiss Sephiroth boots and renounce the perfection that is Demetheus's pecs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T10:26:21-07:00","id":1206939,"title":"","content":"Or of course you could just use Twisted Words Technique.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T10:27:50-07:00","id":1206940,"title":"","content":"Are you talking about yours or someone else's? <br /> <br /> If you're attempting to degrade a defining intimacy of someone's then you need either a major or defining intimacy that supports the degrade attempt. This does not mean they need to disagree with or contradict the defining intimacy. If you're trying to remove a person's loyalty to their house you don't have to operate from them having a desire brutally murder all of them, you just need something important to the person that you can use make them care less about house loyalty. <br /> <br /> Also defining intimacies don't prevent the creation of intimacies that go against them. It is just unlikely for it to crop up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T10:29:03-07:00","id":1206942,"title":"","content":"Yeah, they just give +4 Resolve to things that are against them. But 8 dice of excellency should cover that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T11:02:25-07:00","id":1206951,"title":"","content":"hmmn just thought, if a Dragon blooded has a defining intimacy to his house and a major intimacy to the realm, and learns his house is commiting treason how will that likely play out I know add up the bonuses and penaltys is what it says<br /> <br /> safe to say that could be volatile?<br /> <br /> and even if he sides with his house he might want the people commiting treason brought to justice and see his house publicly abhor what they did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T12:30:05-07:00","id":1206981,"title":"","content":"any charms that explicitly helps with attacking defining intimacys?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T12:46:42-07:00","id":1206988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1206926-how-to-weaken-a-defining-intimacy?p=1206951#post1206951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hmmn just thought, if a Dragon blooded has a defining intimacy to his house and a major intimacy to the realm, and learns his house is commiting treason how will that likely play out I know add up the bonuses and penaltys is what it says<br /> <br /> safe to say that could be volatile?<br /> <br /> and even if he sides with his house he might want the people commiting treason brought to justice and see his house publicly abhor what they did.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's a hero with conflicted desires, clashing principles! A staple of literature to make the hero suffer <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T09:39:00-07:00","id":1207303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1206926-how-to-weaken-a-defining-intimacy?p=1206951#post1206951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hmmn just thought, if a Dragon blooded has a defining intimacy to his house and a major intimacy to the realm, and learns his house is commiting treason how will that likely play out I know add up the bonuses and penaltys is what it says<br /> <br /> safe to say that could be volatile?<br /> <br /> and even if he sides with his house he might want the people commiting treason brought to justice and see his house publicly abhor what they did.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Who says those two Intimacies are even conflicting?<br /> <br /> He has a Defining Intimacy towards his House, NOT the traitorous members of it... and he doesn't want to see his House end up the next Iselsi!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5771-krata-lightblade","name":"Krata Lightblade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5771_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T10:08:42-07:00","id":1207311,"title":"","content":"As others have said, whether two intimacies conflict is contextual; as circumstances change, two intimacies that don\u2019t conflict at one point might begin to conflict later. So you pretty much need to give them a Major Intimacy that doesn\u2019t seem to conflict with the Defining Intimacy you want to erode, and then arrange circumstances such that they come into conflict. You can then attempt to use the Major Intimacy to erode the Defining.<br /> <br /> This is pretty difficult!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T10:14:41-07:00","id":1207314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krata Lightblade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1206926-how-to-weaken-a-defining-intimacy?p=1207303#post1207303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Who says those two Intimacies are even conflicting?<br /> <br /> He has a Defining Intimacy towards his House, NOT the traitorous members of it... and he doesn't want to see his House end up the next Iselsi!</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d say that, while it\u2019s normally up to a player to define what his character\u2019s intimacies mean, if another character wanted to use this situation in order to pit the first character\u2019s pro-house intimacy against his pro-Realm intimacy or vice verse, it would not be okay for the first player to argue \u201cAh, but the intimacy is to my House, not traitorous members within it, therefore there\u2019s no conflict.\u201d<br /> <br /> That said, \u201cThere\u2019s no conflict\u201d would be a good justification for if this attempt at social influence failed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T10:30:53-07:00","id":1207318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1206926-how-to-weaken-a-defining-intimacy?p=1206981#post1206981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">any charms that explicitly helps with attacking defining intimacys?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T10:38:13-07:00","id":1207322,"title":"","content":"The entire point of Intimacies, or a big part of it, anyway, is to make it more difficult to change people's minds than just throw a giant pile of social dice at them and watch their viewpoints erode.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T15:01:34-07:00","id":1207416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1206926-how-to-weaken-a-defining-intimacy?p=1207311#post1207311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As others have said, whether two intimacies conflict is contextual; as circumstances change, two intimacies that don\u2019t conflict at one point might begin to conflict later. So you pretty much need to give them a Major Intimacy that doesn\u2019t seem to conflict with the Defining Intimacy you want to erode, and then arrange circumstances such that they come into conflict. You can then attempt to use the Major Intimacy to erode the Defining.<br /> <br /> This is pretty difficult!</div> </div> </div> </div>I do really like how it encourages the kinds of tragic stories we like to tell about this kind of thing, from <i>Othello</i> all the way down to <i>Revenge of the Sith</i>.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3457-matthias","name":"Matthias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T02:40:03-07:00","id":1207592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1206926-how-to-weaken-a-defining-intimacy?p=1206936#post1206936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To weaken a defining intimacy, you only need them to have a major intimacy that opposes it, not defining.<br /> <br /> Of course, how likely is it that they'll have a major intimacy that opposes their defining intimacy? Not likely. Though it is possible.<br /> For example, if an Immaculate Monk had a defining intimacy of &quot;All Anathema are evil&quot; and a Major Intimacy to &quot;my friend Righteous Fox&quot;, but then learns that Righteous Fox is an anathema, you could use this to weaken their belief that &quot;All Anathema are evil.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now, if they don't have any intimacies that oppose their defining intimacy at all... that's very difficult.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember that they only need to <i>think</i> the intimacies are in opposition. For example, in the situation you mentioned, you could trick them into believing their friend was Anathema. Notably, even if they discover the argument was a lie after the fact, they can't automatically get their intimacy back (although they'll probably work to repair it) - after all, your heart isn't a logic engine, so a moment of doubt can't be erased even if you know it's based on lies.<br /> <br /> It's also often possible to introduce conflicts between intimacies through argument. For example, if someone has intimacies of &quot;Loyalty to the Realm&quot; and &quot;Justice&quot; (not an uncommon pairing, I'd imagine, among more righteous Immaculate Monks), all you have to do to weaken their loyalty to the Realm is show that it is unjust.<br /> <br /> This requires some judgment calls on eg. whether something is sufficient to force a conflict, but my inclination would be to allow any such argument from the players that makes for an interesting story, which generally means it's fine as long as the argument isn't totally absurd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T03:54:30-07:00","id":1207599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1206926-how-to-weaken-a-defining-intimacy?p=1206942#post1206942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, they just give +4 Resolve to things that are against them. But 8 dice of excellency should cover that.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to the core, if multiple intimacies apply the bonus stack so its actually a +2 presumably","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5296-xeliffo","name":"xeliffo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T05:03:47-07:00","id":1207610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1206926-how-to-weaken-a-defining-intimacy?p=1206981#post1206981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">any charms that explicitly helps with attacking defining intimacys?</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't seem like a Solar trick, attacking a defining intimacy without suitable leverage would be like rewriting their Motivation in 2e. Maybe through sorcery or Exalt types whose powers are a lot less respectful of the notion of free will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T05:14:52-07:00","id":1207614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1206926-how-to-weaken-a-defining-intimacy?p=1207610#post1207610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exalt types whose powers are a lot less respectful of the notion of free will.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are Solars particularly respectful of that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T05:38:57-07:00","id":1207622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1206926-how-to-weaken-a-defining-intimacy?p=1207614#post1207614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are Solars particularly respectful of that?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Abyssals? Infernals?<br /> <br /> I can definitely imagine Abyssal charms that let you attack intimacies much more easily, bringing someone down to a path of nihilism and nothing-matters-ism.<br /> <br /> The old GSPs drew on the power of She Who Lives In Her Name, and could incorporate people into a perfected hierarchy regardless of what they wanted.<br /> <br /> The new ones- whom we know little about, but whom I like the idea of them as 'Solars, but as they were at the height of the First Age and in the depths of their corruption, glorious and terrible' could also easily have all manner of mind whammy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T05:52:42-07:00","id":1207625,"title":"","content":"Also Raksha. Leaving people as hollow shells of themselves is a big part of what they do.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T06:45:52-07:00","id":1207634,"title":"","content":"Certainly I think those are all character types that could have Charms to effectively undermine or subvert Intimacies, but I would attribute that more to their corrosive or beguiling nature, rather than contrasting with Solars or anybody else having any particular Essential respect for free will.<br /> <br /> \u200bMind, considering the definition of a Defining Intimacy and the manner in which it interacts with social influence mechanics, there's something mildly amusing in a conversation revolving around it bringing in the very concept of free will in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T07:06:51-07:00","id":1207640,"title":"","content":"I know Worshipful Lackey acquisition's effect's are temporary.<br /> <br /> But is it good for making people listen to you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T07:40:40-07:00","id":1207657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1206926-how-to-weaken-a-defining-intimacy?p=1207634#post1207634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Certainly I think those are all character types that could have Charms to effectively undermine or subvert Intimacies, but I would attribute that more to their corrosive or beguiling nature, rather than contrasting with Solars or anybody else having any particular Essential respect for free will.<br /> <br /> \u200bMind, considering the definition of a Defining Intimacy and the manner in which it interacts with social influence mechanics, there's something mildly amusing in a conversation revolving around it bringing in the very concept of free will in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing that complicates this talk a bit is that in the real world we have people who managed to talk others into extreme behaviours, sometimes very quickly.<br /> Suicide cults, rapidly-formed riots, the stuff.<br /> <br /> Outside of stuff the game generally labels as &quot;psyche&quot; that scary, powerful persuasion exalts can pull off has parallels IRL. So, barring those exceptions, it's less that exalts overwhelm free will and more that it's rather easy to make an exalt like Girolamo Savonarola, Charles Manson or Luther King. That or you redefine free will, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T10:31:14-07:00","id":1207695,"title":"","content":"Why is it that sociopath's have almost magical ability to control people?<br /> <br /> It's hard to quantify.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T10:54:04-07:00","id":1207704,"title":"","content":"Also remember that you can just use Celestial Bliss Trick to give someone a defining tie towards you, then use that to weaken whatever you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T11:12:27-07:00","id":1207714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1206926-how-to-weaken-a-defining-intimacy?p=1207704#post1207704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also remember that you can just use Celestial Bliss Trick to give someone a defining tie towards you, then use that to weaken whatever you want.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWell, whatever might be opposed specifically by lust.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T13:48:57-07:00","id":1207747,"title":"","content":"And also, a true master of manipulation would be using incite to create emotions to exploit, and Bargains to get other to do those little favors that distances one from his usual social circles, limiting external factors. They're also likely to use their existing followers to bombard the target and drain its Willpower (that is actually a pretty good description of the first half of love-bombing actually...)<br /> <br /> Actually it's not that real-world manipulators are beyond the scope of the system, so much as they play the system to the hilt","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3657-sagara","name":"Sagara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3657_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T21:13:46-07:00","id":1207870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1206926-how-to-weaken-a-defining-intimacy?p=1207714#post1207714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bWell, whatever might be opposed specifically by lust.</div> </div> </div> </div>My feeling is that most of the time, an intimacy towards you can be forced into conflict with almost anything. &quot;Choose between me and X&quot; is pretty straightforward and omni-applicable.<br /> <br /> And it's something with a lot of mythological cachet - &quot;the beautiful seductress who makes you choose between her and your country&quot; is a pretty common trope, say. I think it's intentional that CBT can be used to sway someone from nearly any ideal or course. The drawback is that you have to actually get them to sleep with you, of course. But my reading is that the charm comes from a mythological cachet where love (or lust, yes, although these sorts of stories rarely make the distinction) can be the downfall of essentially any principle or loyalty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T21:22:36-07:00","id":1207873,"title":"","content":"Pretty much. You still have to force a very specific context to oppose the intimacy, but it's strong like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T02:42:53-07:00","id":1208780,"title":"","content":"It's important to remember that while social charms aren't a distinct thing that someone can observe and go &quot;He used the Celestial Bliss Trick! I can't trust a thing he says now&quot; but-<br /> if someone walks in your life one day, you have incredible sex then before you get chance to cuddle goes &quot;...its me or your mom, go snap her neck if you ever want me to look at you again&quot; a defining intimacy doesn't blind you to the fact he just appeared in your life and expects you to murder people for him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T03:10:44-07:00","id":1208787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1206926-how-to-weaken-a-defining-intimacy?p=1208780#post1208780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's important to remember that while social charms aren't a distinct thing that someone can observe and go &quot;He used the Celestial Bliss Trick! I can't trust a thing he says now&quot; but-<br /> if someone walks in your life one day, you have incredible sex then before you get chance to cuddle goes &quot;...its me or your mom, go snap her neck if you ever want me to look at you again&quot; a defining intimacy doesn't blind you to the fact he just appeared in your life and expects you to murder people for him.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which would be grounds for weakening the intimacy at the end of the scene, though I'm not sure how that rule would interact with the specific magic of CBT (heh, I am amused by this acronym).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/855-magistrate","name":"Magistrate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T05:33:22-07:00","id":1208814,"title":"","content":"Which makes all the difference between a cunning manipulator and a dumb one. I certainly know about half my players would do the latter...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T06:56:35-07:00","id":1208837,"title":"","content":"I notice DBs have several charms that let you instill Major intimacies, rather than the usual Minor. Presumably the target can still spend a WP to not get a new intimacy, but it's much easier than giving them a minor, giving them a second minor to support the first, and using stronger evidence to boost the first to major.<br /> <br /> If you give them a major intimacy that opposes their defining intimacy, then you can use it weaken their defining intimacy.<br /> <br /> Still not a totally direct method, but it does make it easier at least.<br /> <br /> Of course, these charms are quite restrictive in terms of what major intimacies, but they're still useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T07:08:34-07:00","id":1208845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1206926-how-to-weaken-a-defining-intimacy?p=1207870#post1207870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My feeling is that most of the time, an intimacy towards you can be forced into conflict with almost anything. &quot;Choose between me and X&quot; is pretty straightforward and omni-applicable.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYeah, I'm not going to run with that interpretation, because it takes the variety and complexity of the social system and turns it into a crude joke, so I hate it.<br /> <br /> \u200bAt the <i>very least</i>, there needs to be some context or setup that would lead the person you're speaking to to buy that ultimatum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T03:32:24-07:00","id":1209966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magistrate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1206926-how-to-weaken-a-defining-intimacy?p=1208787#post1208787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which would be grounds for weakening the intimacy at the end of the scene, though I'm not sure how that rule would interact with the specific magic of CBT (heh, I am amused by this acronym).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Join Battle is a valid response. The fact he thinks you'll kill family members for another round is strong evidence that this was more than great sex with a guy who turned out to be an asshole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T21:36:45-07:00","id":1210275,"title":"","content":"Reading through some of the rules earlier* and the whole use CBS then give the ultimatum of me or defining intimacy would be unacceptable influence as presented. Its a demand to completely abandon a defining intimacy. CBS can be used as leverage for weakening said defining intimacy, you just wouldn't be able to get a DB to go from being defined by loyalty to their family to decide to completely drop it for 3 minutes of really good sex.<br /> <br /> *Was looking for examples and rules for traps if anyone knows where those are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T02:22:19-07:00","id":1210337,"title":"","content":"I'd imagine in my example your mom is a major intimacy, you care about her way more than most things but it's unlikely she dominates every aspect of your life unless she's the family matriarch or there's a serious case of smothering going on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_lin